<div class="analytics-empty">
  <h1>📊 Sessions Analytics Dashboard</h1>

  <div class="empty-state">
    <h2>No Data Available</h2>
    <p>The analytics dashboard requires events.db to be populated with session data.</p>

    <h3>To populate the database:</h3>

    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step">
        <h4>Option 1: Analyze existing week1 sessions</h4>
        <p>From the project root:</p>
        <pre>cd week2_capable
python3 measure_baseline.py .boukensha/sessions/SESSION_ID.jsonl .boukensha</pre>
        <p>This will backfill events.db from an existing JSONL session log.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="step">
        <h4>Option 2: Run the agent with EventStore</h4>
        <p>In your agent script:</p>
        <pre>from boukensha.observability import EventStore

store = EventStore()
store.attach(logger)
# Now run the agent; events written live to .boukensha/events.db</pre>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p><a href="/analytics" class="btn">Refresh</a></p>
  </div>

